4, 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 12 and 15 is read as qualifying the Horror Factor save only: +1 at level one and one at_level entry for each later level. || SKILLS: base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Dragonese is a named row at 90, per_level 0. Atlantean has no catalog row, so it is a pick from Language: Other at +40 (90%), the note naming the language. Math: Basic is Mathematics: Basic; Tracking (humanoids) is Tracking (people). W.P. Archery and Targeting is W.P. Archery, as the Warrior stores it. The two Ancient and two Modern W.P. picks are category picks whose notes say which; the catalog files every W.P. in one category. || HAND TO HAND: Martial Arts granted, Assassin offered at no cost, nothing else offered. || RELATED and SECONDARY: the Staphra Warrior''s lists as production stores them (printed 92-93), copied whole; six related at level one plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 13; two secondary at level one plus one at levels 2, 4, 7, 10 and 14. || EQUIPMENT: catalog rows by slug, as the Warrior stores them; satchel is purse-satchel and communicator is walkie-talkie. The medium and heavy body armor (60 and 100 M.D.C., no stat block), the weapon per W.P. with E-clips, the S.D.C. double-bladed spear, the lesser Bio-Wizard pistol and the officers'' staves are prose in restrictions. || MONEY: player characters 2D6x100 credits; slaves none, a restriction line. || NOT STORED: height, weight, life span, habitat, slave market value (100,000-300,000 credits), allies and enemies are in the body."
